# Mach-O export list: only the WFX entry points leave the dylib.
#
# The counterpart of fsplugin.map on ELF, and needed for the same reason.
# -fvisibility=hidden covers our own code, but RTTI symbols (__ZTI.../__ZTS...)
# for the std::function instantiations this plugin uses have vague linkage and
# are emitted as weak *default-visibility* globals, which -fvisibility=hidden
# does not touch. On arm64 they happen to be optimised away; on x86_64 they are
# not, and they showed up in the export table.
#
# Nothing crosses the dylib boundary as a C++ type -- fsplugin.cpp's exports are
# extern "C" and each catches its own exceptions -- so RTTI never needs to be
# matched against another image, and hiding it is safe.
_Fs*
